WEBVTT

00:01.501 --> 00:03.044
<i>In the present time,</i>

00:03.128 --> 00:06.840
<i>With VR headgear,</i>
<i>you can go into a virtual world</i>

00:06.923 --> 00:10.510
<i>and play as the resident of that world.</i>

00:10.593 --> 00:14.597
<i>VR Full-Dive games are</i>
<i>at the height of their popularity.</i>

00:15.890 --> 00:18.768
<i>And stands above all other games,</i>

00:18.852 --> 00:22.897
<i>With over thirty million</i>
<i>players worldwide,</i>

00:22.981 --> 00:25.567
<i>There exists a god-tier game.</i>

00:25.650 --> 00:27.360
<i>And the name of that game is…</i>

00:27.444 --> 00:30.030
<i>Shangri-La Frontier.</i>

00:35.785 --> 00:36.870
<i>However…</i>

00:39.414 --> 00:41.583
<i>After several heartbreaking events,</i>

00:41.666 --> 00:44.043
<i>Sunraku stopped playing SLF,</i>

00:44.127 --> 00:46.880
<i>but instead, a robot action game</i>
<i>in which you can customize</i>

00:46.963 --> 00:49.716
<i>and fight with mechs that came down</i>
<i>from the sky called "Nephilim."</i>

00:49.799 --> 00:51.551
<i>Nephilim Hollow.</i>

00:52.552 --> 00:55.930
(Red or Green?)
I want to always stay incomplete Yeah

00:56.014 --> 00:59.392
(Red or Green?)
Lalala Red Light? Green Light?

00:59.476 --> 01:02.771
(Red or Green?)
No, not yet This is not my limit Yeah

01:02.854 --> 01:06.316
(Red or Green?)
Lalala Red Light? Green Light?

01:13.156 --> 01:16.534
I even miss the scar now

01:16.618 --> 01:19.329
It's not sparkling, it's glaring

01:19.412 --> 01:20.997
(Chase me! Chase me!)

01:21.081 --> 01:23.374
Even when I catch you

01:23.458 --> 01:26.795
Your robe simply swings

01:26.878 --> 01:29.506
Be it love or hate, it's all the same

01:29.589 --> 01:33.009
They'll be nutrition once I swallow them

01:33.092 --> 01:36.471
It's a great answer that
even shines the uncertain truth

01:36.554 --> 01:39.974
I will bloom profusely over and over

01:40.058 --> 01:43.937
Moonlight
Split the cloud, show me your face

01:44.020 --> 01:46.689
(Let's dance lala lalala)

01:46.773 --> 01:50.902
Tonight
Light up the darkness and make a sound

01:50.985 --> 01:53.488
(Let's dance A lonely dance)

01:53.571 --> 01:57.659
I want to keep it all to myself,
loving it completely

01:57.742 --> 02:01.704
I have no more doubts in me
Oh Yeah!

02:01.788 --> 02:04.541
I won't give this away, I am the QUEEN

02:04.624 --> 02:08.044
I will not be satisfied,
I will not be disturbed Yeah

02:14.884 --> 02:18.680
(Red or Green?)
I have no limit Yeah

02:29.607 --> 02:32.318
I don't see traces of him
escaping with his booster…

02:40.160 --> 02:42.078
No way, that Nephilim…!

02:42.162 --> 02:44.289
<i>Rust! Get away from there!</i>

02:49.961 --> 02:50.962
It's over.

02:55.967 --> 03:01.139
(Like Lions Against Rabbits,
A Crab's Pizza Cutter Against The Phoenix)

03:01.222 --> 03:02.765
What was that?!

03:02.849 --> 03:04.893
He got Twinewing's arm!

03:04.976 --> 03:06.978
When, and how did he get up there?!

03:13.318 --> 03:17.238
Man, I thought I nailed
that one, but you dodged it.

03:20.575 --> 03:22.911
Mordo! What did he do?!

03:22.994 --> 03:25.622
<i>Why did the Fiddler Crab</i>
<i>get so close to me?</i>

03:25.705 --> 03:28.041
<i>He was definitely on the surface</i>
<i>at that moment!</i>

03:28.124 --> 03:30.001
<i>There's no way I wouldn't</i>
<i>be able to notice him move!</i>

03:30.460 --> 03:33.004
The booster effect is a bait!

03:33.087 --> 03:33.922
<i>A bait?</i>

03:34.005 --> 03:37.258
I confirmed it the moment
his camo came off.

03:37.342 --> 03:40.470
He switched his leg parts
with Anti-Gravity Legs!

03:41.012 --> 03:42.472
He switched them?

03:44.641 --> 03:45.808
False Legs!

03:45.892 --> 03:47.477
That's right.

03:47.560 --> 03:50.939
It's a new Nephilim type
added two weeks ago.

03:51.022 --> 03:56.653
It has a unique mechanism that lets
you transform between two leg parts.

03:56.736 --> 03:59.489
But in exchange,
it eats up a lot of energy,

03:59.572 --> 04:03.409
and the weight of two leg
parts hurts your mobility.

04:04.118 --> 04:08.331
It has so many disadvantages that
nobody uses them in competitive play.

04:09.290 --> 04:12.085
This is the first time
we've played against one.

04:12.877 --> 04:14.462
I'm sorry, Rust.

04:14.545 --> 04:17.924
I should've noticed it after
seeing his unusual leg parts.

04:18.967 --> 04:20.760
<i>No, even with Anti-Gravity Legs,</i>

04:20.843 --> 04:24.722
<i>flying that distance should've</i>
<i>generated dust clouds.</i>

04:24.806 --> 04:27.600
<i>Right there! Better luck</i>
<i>next time, Fiddler Crab!</i>

04:31.646 --> 04:35.984
<i>Which means he transformed</i>
<i>his legs while dodging my attack</i>

04:36.067 --> 04:40.822
<i>and approached my Crimson Twinewing</i>
<i>by jumping the moment my missiles hit</i>

04:40.905 --> 04:45.285
<i>and hiding within the dust</i>
<i>clouds the explosion generates.</i>

04:53.668 --> 04:54.961
Rust?

04:56.879 --> 05:00.591
Well, even if someone else got the idea,
only Sunraku could actually do it.

05:00.675 --> 05:01.301
Huh?

05:01.384 --> 05:02.385
What do you mean?

05:03.094 --> 05:05.763
Looks like the cat's out of the bag.

05:09.100 --> 05:10.601
What now?

05:10.685 --> 05:12.228
Crimson Twinewing.

05:15.940 --> 05:18.609
The camo will go away over time.

05:19.068 --> 05:21.612
Aim for when he's visible
and charging up his camo!

05:21.696 --> 05:25.116
Just stay up high enough where
his anti-grav can't reach you!

05:28.244 --> 05:29.370
Rust?

05:37.754 --> 05:39.922
Rust? What are you doing?

05:43.301 --> 05:46.763
Heh, not taking the safe,
boring route, huh?

05:47.472 --> 05:50.266
I figured you were like that.

05:53.352 --> 05:56.272
Come at me from wherever.
I will take you on.

05:57.065 --> 05:58.149
But…

05:59.317 --> 06:02.570
Don't you underestimate me, Sunraku.

06:02.653 --> 06:05.239
And you better not get
the wrong idea here, Rust.

06:05.823 --> 06:08.659
The Fiddle Crab's real hunt
has only just started!

06:09.243 --> 06:12.872
Rust… Are you really
going to take him head-on?!

06:12.955 --> 06:16.292
Hey, maybe Sunraku actually has a chance?!

06:16.375 --> 06:17.877
Yeah! Go get her!

06:17.960 --> 06:20.922
Let us see Rust's new Nephilim!

06:21.005 --> 06:24.509
If you make even one mistake,
you'll blow your chance, Sunraku.

06:34.018 --> 06:35.770
It's pointless.

06:35.853 --> 06:38.189
I don't need to even read the
movement of the dust clouds.

06:38.272 --> 06:42.568
Your camo will shut down the
moment you enter your attack motion.

06:43.111 --> 06:46.114
Catching that single moment is all I need!

07:04.674 --> 07:05.758
The pincher!

07:05.842 --> 07:07.385
She got it!

07:09.679 --> 07:13.975
A super high-speed counter
using an asymmetric booster blast.

07:14.058 --> 07:15.351
Nice one.

07:15.435 --> 07:18.312
But I accomplished what I aim for.

07:18.396 --> 07:20.815
Let me show you my trump card!

07:20.898 --> 07:23.151
Rust! He's got a Capture Net!

07:26.696 --> 07:28.739
That's your "trump card"?

07:28.823 --> 07:32.201
It seems you really do
underestimate me, huh, Sunraku!

07:33.202 --> 07:34.954
She's going for a finisher!

07:35.288 --> 07:36.956
Sunraku…

07:37.039 --> 07:40.209
Fiddler Crab's trump card
is a win-or-nothing kinda deal.

07:40.585 --> 07:41.502
What?

07:41.586 --> 07:44.630
It means I must make sure I land the hit.

07:44.714 --> 07:49.552
The problem with fighting Rust is
her unpredictable high-speed mobility.

07:49.635 --> 07:51.345
What makes it possible are…

07:51.429 --> 07:54.682
the trajectory-changing boosters
strapped to her unit's shoulders.

07:55.183 --> 07:57.477
Which means if I can
destroy those, at least,

07:57.560 --> 08:02.231
she can only do straight maneuvers with
her high-powered main booster on her back.

08:02.815 --> 08:04.233
In other words…

08:05.610 --> 08:08.738
I lean lead her to dodge
in the direction I want!

08:12.408 --> 08:17.163
I called this "Fiddler Crab," but
I actually got one more pincher.

08:20.583 --> 08:22.919
Eat this! Pizza Cutter Wing!

08:25.755 --> 08:27.590
Sunraku!

08:42.313 --> 08:43.231
Heh!

08:43.314 --> 08:45.775
Heavy-weight unit
against light-weight unit.

08:45.858 --> 08:49.195
Needless to say which of them
has more advantage in a double KO.

09:04.043 --> 09:07.004
<i>Winner, Fiddler Crab!</i>

09:08.798 --> 09:12.260
He… He did it!

09:12.343 --> 09:15.596
Sunraku, that guy!
He actually defeated Rust!

09:15.680 --> 09:17.557
What a fight that was!

09:17.640 --> 09:20.685
Now we can finally
see Rust's new Nephilim!

09:23.896 --> 09:26.649
(Winner: Fiddler Crab)

09:27.733 --> 09:31.654
The Bookmaker, the optical
camo, and the Fake Legs…

09:31.737 --> 09:34.949
The Capture Net,
and the saw on his back…

09:35.032 --> 09:38.369
That's a lot to process
in just a few minutes.

09:42.290 --> 09:45.418
Woohoo! That felt GREAT!

09:45.501 --> 09:49.630
It's like I'm drinkin' victory
champagne from a two-liter bottle!

09:49.714 --> 09:52.508
Wo, wo, wo, wonderful!

09:55.261 --> 09:56.762
Whaddya think, Rust?

09:56.846 --> 09:59.307
This is what I call "operation
shut down your operator

09:59.390 --> 10:01.350
with too much data and
force you into one-on-one"!

10:01.434 --> 10:03.728
Yeah, you beat Crimson
Twinewing, I admit it.

10:03.811 --> 10:04.937
But I'm not done with you yet!

10:05.021 --> 10:07.356
Now we both got one win,
one loss, and a draw.

10:07.440 --> 10:09.650
It's not decided yet! Next time…

10:09.734 --> 10:11.652
Um, sorry to bust your bubble…

10:11.736 --> 10:16.198
I accomplished what I came here for,
so I wanna go back to my main game now.

10:16.282 --> 10:17.533
Your main game?

10:18.034 --> 10:21.704
Wait! Didn't you come back
so you can focus on <i>Nephilim</i>?!

10:21.787 --> 10:24.999
Don't tell me you
gonna stop playing again…

10:25.541 --> 10:27.710
Well, yeah, for a while.

10:27.793 --> 10:30.171
I'll pop back in before long, I promise.

10:31.047 --> 10:33.674
Whoa, are you serious, Sunraku?

10:33.758 --> 10:36.344
Right after things
just got exciting again?

10:36.427 --> 10:39.722
The game is so full of life now
after you came.

10:39.805 --> 10:44.268
I'm sure things will be more fun
if you can keep logging in…

10:44.644 --> 10:48.564
Umm, I get you, but, well…

10:49.106 --> 10:50.316
That's not good…

10:51.025 --> 10:51.817
What?

10:52.318 --> 10:54.236
That's not good at all!

10:54.320 --> 10:56.947
You better log in tomorrow!
And the day after that, too!

10:57.031 --> 10:58.824
Whoa, calm down!

10:58.908 --> 11:00.409
I'm here to work off
my frustration from

11:00.493 --> 11:02.578
being the only one who can't
use the robots in <i>SLF</i>.

11:05.164 --> 11:07.124
Robot in <i>SLF</i>?

11:07.208 --> 11:08.417
Ah, crap!

11:08.834 --> 11:11.170
So your main game is <i>SLF</i>?

11:11.587 --> 11:14.715
No, never mind that! Forget it!

11:14.799 --> 11:16.175
<i>SLF</i>, huh.

11:18.052 --> 11:21.597
I used to play <i>Shangri-La Frontier</i> before.

11:23.140 --> 11:28.437
But no matter how long I play, I couldn't
find any robot that players can use.

11:30.022 --> 11:32.358
But they really <i>do</i> exist, huh?!

11:33.484 --> 11:36.070
Sunraku! Let's make a deal!

11:36.153 --> 11:36.946
What?!

11:37.279 --> 11:41.450
Depending on the information
you give me about those robots…

11:43.369 --> 11:45.538
I wouldn't mind telling you
about the Unique Scenario

11:45.621 --> 11:47.957
that leads to the Unique Monster
Ctarnidd of the Abyss.

11:50.918 --> 11:52.837
The abyss…

12:01.512 --> 12:03.347
All right, nobody's around.

12:03.431 --> 12:05.724
Did we really need to change location?

12:06.725 --> 12:10.479
There might be other players who
also play SLF besides you guys.

12:10.813 --> 12:13.566
Information on Unique Monsters
is really valuable, y'know?

12:14.108 --> 12:15.568
Yeah, I know that.

12:16.444 --> 12:19.822
Well, how about we
start our deal right away?

12:21.532 --> 12:22.575
Of course.

12:22.992 --> 12:26.036
On our side is information
on a Unique Scenario that

12:26.120 --> 12:29.081
leads to the Unique Monster
Ctarnidd of the Abyss.

12:29.457 --> 12:34.837
On yours is information on robots that
players can control somewhere in <i>SLF</i>.

12:35.504 --> 12:38.716
And our deal is to trade
those information. Is that right?

12:39.592 --> 12:42.011
<i>According to the Professor</i>
<i>from the lore clan…</i>

12:42.094 --> 12:44.138
<i>Ctarnidd of the Abyss.</i>

12:44.221 --> 12:48.517
<i>A Unique Monster that appears in</i>
<i>the ocean with the shape of an octopus.</i>

12:48.601 --> 12:52.396
<i>However, no player has</i>
<i>actually seen it in person.</i>

12:52.480 --> 12:57.109
<i>All our info about it comes</i>
<i>from half-crazed NPCs.</i>

12:57.818 --> 13:01.614
<i>And Rust knows about a</i>
<i>unique scenario that leads to it?</i>

13:02.573 --> 13:03.782
What?

13:03.866 --> 13:04.950
Nothing.

13:05.034 --> 13:10.039
I just didn't expect to hear words like
"Unique Monster" in other games like this.

13:10.122 --> 13:12.541
Are you saying you don't find us credible?

13:12.625 --> 13:16.545
We've played <i>SLF</i> quite
a lot ourselves, you know.

13:16.629 --> 13:19.840
Well, it's not that I'm
doubting you or anything.

13:20.382 --> 13:23.719
It's just that Unique Scenarios
that lead to Unique Monsters in <i>SLF</i>

13:23.802 --> 13:26.639
are intricately constructed.

13:27.348 --> 13:32.269
So until I can be sure
how useful your info is,

13:32.353 --> 13:34.647
I can't give you my end of the deal.

13:35.231 --> 13:37.024
You want us to go first?

13:37.107 --> 13:38.817
You're being awfully cautious.

13:38.901 --> 13:45.449
Actually, the sci-fi equipment and
robots I got aren't exclusively mine.

13:45.533 --> 13:47.910
I share their possession with two others.

13:50.246 --> 13:54.416
So I can't tell you anything
unless I can convince them.

13:55.292 --> 13:59.838
<i>And one misstep, who knows</i>
<i>what they'll do with me.</i>

13:59.922 --> 14:02.258
And whether or not you can convince them

14:02.341 --> 14:06.178
depends on the info we have,
is that what you're saying?

14:06.512 --> 14:08.013
Exactly.

14:08.097 --> 14:09.265
Fine.

14:09.348 --> 14:10.140
Mordo.

14:10.224 --> 14:11.141
One sec.

14:12.476 --> 14:16.855
In the fifth town, Fifticia,
there's a Unique Scenario

14:16.939 --> 14:18.983
titled "Pierce the Disciple of the Abyss."

14:19.567 --> 14:23.028
In it, an NPC named
"Self-Styled Great Pirate Stude"

14:23.112 --> 14:24.989
ask the player the pursue
a "ghost ship" where…

14:25.072 --> 14:26.699
Mordo, was it?

14:26.782 --> 14:28.534
No need to be so formal.

14:28.617 --> 14:32.162
Uh, yes. I mean, sure.

14:32.246 --> 14:34.415
Then I'll continue.

14:37.543 --> 14:41.964
We accepted this scenario
over in Fifticia,

14:42.047 --> 14:47.803
and that's where we were told
about the ghost ship, "Crying Innsman."

14:48.304 --> 14:50.723
According to
Self-Styled Great Pirate Stude,

14:50.806 --> 14:55.561
the ghost ship will offer its kidnapped
inhabitants to the "Master of the Abyss."

14:56.061 --> 14:58.564
The Master of the Abyss…

14:59.231 --> 15:01.191
So you haven't finished the scenario yet?

15:01.275 --> 15:03.444
Yeah, we've only accepted it.

15:03.527 --> 15:08.824
That was when Rust said she quit
since we're not finding any robots.

15:11.285 --> 15:14.747
What do you think?
Is it useful enough?

15:16.457 --> 15:19.126
Close, but it lacks anything decisive.

15:21.128 --> 15:26.967
Unique Scenarios that directly connect to
Unique Monster have "EX" attached to them.

15:27.051 --> 15:28.260
EX?

15:29.011 --> 15:33.223
Perhaps that "Pierce the Disciple
of the Abyss" Unique Scenario

15:33.307 --> 15:36.435
is one that leads to an
EX Unique Scenario.

15:36.518 --> 15:39.688
So you're saying what we
have now is still too weak?

15:41.273 --> 15:45.361
But in other words, if we finished
"Pierce the Disciple of the Abyss"

15:45.444 --> 15:50.240
and trigger an EX Unique Scenario,
we'll have what we need?

15:51.617 --> 15:52.743
Yeah.

15:53.369 --> 15:56.163
<i>If I play my cards right,</i>
<i>I'll have the opportunity</i>

15:56.246 --> 16:00.000
<i>to play another EX Unique Scenario</i>
<i>aside from Vorpal Epic!</i>

16:00.334 --> 16:02.044
Let's keep the ball rolling.

16:02.127 --> 16:05.756
I'll be happy to help you out with
that ghost ship Unique Scenario.

16:06.090 --> 16:07.925
That's reassuring to hear.

16:08.008 --> 16:10.094
Where should we meet up, then?

16:10.177 --> 16:12.304
I say it'll be efficient
if we meet up in Fifticia…

16:12.388 --> 16:13.681
Sunraku.

16:13.764 --> 16:14.765
Hm?

16:16.517 --> 16:20.020
Are you really… quitting <i>Nephilim</i>?

16:20.604 --> 16:21.522
Rust.

16:23.774 --> 16:27.611
I heard that because you won't
switch out until you lose,

16:27.695 --> 16:30.781
you've been using Crimson Twinewing.

16:32.408 --> 16:36.912
It might be a win, loss, and tie, but you
<i>did</i> lose with your Crimson Twinewing.

16:37.579 --> 16:38.372
That's…

16:38.455 --> 16:40.416
Once your new Nephilim…

16:41.083 --> 16:43.919
Once you finished up a new Nephilim…

16:48.048 --> 16:50.426
I'll log back in for you!

16:56.348 --> 16:57.766
Sunraku…

17:11.530 --> 17:13.866
In that case, let's fight right now.

17:15.200 --> 17:18.495
Huh? Eh? What?

17:23.751 --> 17:27.254
This is my new Nephilim, Ashen Antinomy!

17:27.588 --> 17:32.009
(Ashen Antinomy)

17:37.556 --> 17:41.769
Whaaat?! Why you already have one made?!

17:42.811 --> 17:47.024
She actually couldn't hold her urges
and had been working on it on and off.

17:48.192 --> 17:49.943
Damn it!

17:50.027 --> 17:52.529
Where the hell did the three of them go?

17:54.698 --> 17:58.869
Is that bastard really going
to stop playing like this?

17:58.952 --> 17:59.870
I swear I saw them fly this way.

17:59.953 --> 18:01.789
- "On and off" my ass!
I swear I saw them fly this way.

18:01.872 --> 18:04.291
O-Oh, hey! Over there!

18:04.374 --> 18:07.586
What Nephilim is that?
I've never seen that one before.

18:07.669 --> 18:10.923
Hey, isn't that other one
facing it Sunraku's build?

18:11.006 --> 18:12.299
Sure looks like it.

18:12.382 --> 18:15.135
No way, is that Rust?

18:15.761 --> 18:18.138
Is that Rust's new Nephilim?

18:20.641 --> 18:23.560
The right side's built for close range…

18:23.644 --> 18:26.522
And the left side's built for long range.

18:26.605 --> 18:31.944
Man, I was trying to close this off
swiftly with a couple of parting words…

18:32.653 --> 18:37.449
But how can I resist the allure of
fighting a strong opponent like this?!

18:44.581 --> 18:48.585
Still, you already know all the
secrets behind my Fiddler Crab.

18:48.669 --> 18:51.839
Talk about huge advantages.
This is a one-trick pony, after all.

18:51.922 --> 18:56.343
Wanna give up your seat
to those under there, then?

18:57.803 --> 19:01.014
Hey, contact everybody now!
They're gonna miss this!

19:01.098 --> 19:03.851
I'm serious! Rust's using a new build!
Hurry it up!

19:03.934 --> 19:05.602
No, dude, it's City Map B!

19:05.686 --> 19:07.521
Oh, the transport will start!

19:07.604 --> 19:09.231
Rust!

19:09.314 --> 19:14.820
Oh, yeah, those guys were dying to see you
pilot something besides Crimson Twinewing.

19:15.195 --> 19:21.076
Okay, then, let's warp this
up with a bang, shall we?

19:21.368 --> 19:24.079
(Rust challenged you to a duel)

19:26.290 --> 19:28.542
<i>Transporting to spectator area.</i>

19:39.595 --> 19:49.605
Rust! Rust! Rust! Rust!
Rust! Rust! Rust! Rust!

19:50.439 --> 19:54.067
<i>Fiddler Crab versus Ashen Antinomy!</i>

19:54.151 --> 19:56.361
<i>Duel Start!</i>

19:56.653 --> 19:57.946
Let's go!

20:01.867 --> 20:06.413
I'll be back to beat you again,
so wait for me!

20:20.385 --> 20:21.929
Good grief.

20:23.222 --> 20:26.183
Those guys really know
how to entertain me.

20:40.197 --> 20:43.200
(Palace of Rabituza)

20:49.122 --> 20:51.416
What a nice weather.

20:52.584 --> 20:54.836
It's been days now.

20:56.421 --> 20:59.716
Sunraku-san hasn't come back since.

21:02.219 --> 21:04.721
There ye are, Emul.

21:06.265 --> 21:08.767
Ceecrue-oniichan!

21:10.852 --> 21:13.397
I'm glad to see ye doing well, Emul.

21:13.480 --> 21:15.274
Long time no see!

21:15.357 --> 21:17.651
May I ask ye something?

21:17.734 --> 21:20.195
I can't seem to find our father
anywhere in the palace.

21:21.863 --> 21:24.199
Are ye aware where he might be?

21:24.283 --> 21:26.451
I don't know either.

21:27.452 --> 21:28.954
Ah, is that so…

21:29.454 --> 21:31.957
Do you need him for something?

21:32.708 --> 21:36.211
I came across a quite
amazing human recognized

21:36.295 --> 21:39.006
by the Golden Dragon King
Siegwurm, in fact.

21:39.089 --> 21:44.136
Really? There's another great Pioneer
like Sunraku-san out there?

21:44.219 --> 21:47.723
Yes. She's quite a skilled
fighter, I'll have ya know.

21:48.348 --> 21:51.768
I was hoping to introduce
her to our father…

21:52.477 --> 21:54.271
Yes, over here, please.

21:54.980 --> 21:57.316
This is my sister, Emul.

21:57.399 --> 21:59.234
Oh, right, Ceecrue-san.

22:01.486 --> 22:03.739
Nice to meet you, Emul-san.

22:09.161 --> 22:10.787
I'm Akitsuakane!

22:21.923 --> 22:23.759
Can't stop trembling with excitement

22:23.842 --> 22:26.178
Ahhh it's the best feeling ever

22:26.261 --> 22:31.725
It's like when you end up laughing harder
the more you try to hold it in

22:31.808 --> 22:33.018
Well? What about you?

22:33.101 --> 22:36.104
Does your heartbeat throb
as it dances deep down inside?

22:36.188 --> 22:41.401
It's far more terrifying to contemplate a future
that ends without ever having known that feeling

22:41.777 --> 22:45.322
In a world filled with glitches

22:45.405 --> 22:50.911
Telling me not to glitch
is glitched out in itself, right?

22:51.495 --> 22:58.502
Same as ever,
we're still like hungry underdogs

22:59.628 --> 23:02.547
Step to the beat, to the beat

23:02.631 --> 23:04.758
It's a battered and bruised dance

23:04.841 --> 23:09.262
Barefoot and alone, I clench my teeth
and laugh as I kick at the rubble

23:09.346 --> 23:12.099
A paradise in an irreplaceable battlefield

23:12.182 --> 23:14.476
A stage with broken lighting fixture

23:14.559 --> 23:19.231
Suits this idiot perfectly

23:19.314 --> 23:22.609
The moon lights a path to the future

23:22.692 --> 23:26.822
Don't need to be told
I'm incorrigibly lame

23:26.905 --> 23:33.537
The incorrigibly lame-
they're the real deal
